{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And to him</b> — to him was given dominion and glory and kingship, and all the peoples, nations, and tongues shall serve him; his dominion is an everlasting dominion that shall not pass, and his kingship shall not be destroyed. Now we have seen that the angel did not explain to him anything except the fourth beast, and indeed it is so, for the three first beasts the discerning one can know from Daniel's later prophecies. Now you should know that the reason is four beasts, because the four kingdoms were in different directions, and I do not know the reason for the great sea, for all of them were on dry land — perhaps because the soul of the beast that creeps in the great sea is greater than the soul of the beast that is on dry land. This prophecy is at the death of Evil-Merodach and the beginning of Belshazzar. And the lion is the kingdom of Chaldeans. And the Gaon [Saadia] said: this vision concerns a past event, namely the matter of Nebuchadnezzar and 'a man's heart was given to it,' that he returned to his senses — 'this' and 'from my knowledge it is reverted upon him.' And this is not correct in my eyes, for what reason is there to see what has passed and what benefit is there to mention it. And this interpretation: 'the first, like a lion,' is Nebuchadnezzar." "<b>And the eagle's wings</b> — his son Evil-Merodach and his grandson Belshazzar, who was killed." "<b>And it was plucked from the earth</b> — they had already lifted it then; 'it plucked its wings' is in the Holy Language many. And the meaning of 'it was made to stand on two feet like a man, and a man's heart was given to it': the heart of the lion is greater than the heart of man. And the meaning is that the Chaldeans at first tore prey like a lion, and when their king was killed the Chaldeans were brought low and acquired a heart and became like all other men. And Yefet said: the meaning of 'like a man' is that the whole world sees its disgrace. And he interpreted well. And the second beast is the kingdom of Persia, which destroyed the kingdom of the Chaldeans, and it is the one likened to silver in Nebuchadnezzar's dream. And the meaning of 'and it had one side' is that on one side of the kingdom of the Chaldeans Cyrus and Darius killed three great cities. I also saw this written in the book of the kings of Persia forty years ago, and I have forgotten the names of the cities. And this is 'arise, devour much flesh' — from the kingdom of the Chaldeans. And Rav Saadia the Gaon said: this alludes to Ahasuerus, who sent letters to destroy Israel, who are called 'a great and mighty people.' But what reason is there for this interpretation, since Ahasuerus did not take the kingdom of the Chaldeans at first. And the third beast, likened to a leopard, is the kingdom of Greece, beginning with the kingdom of Alexander, who was king over them, and it is the one likened in Nebuchadnezzar's prophecy to bronze, where it is written: 'that it should rule over all the earth,' and so it is written in the prophecy, 'and dominion was given to it.' And this that he said, 'and four wings,' they are the four kings who ruled over the kingdom of Alexander, and this is a known matter, and thus he said: 'and four appeared in place of it.' And it is written there, 'to the four winds of heaven,' as he said: 'four heads to the beast,' and there I shall explain it. And the fourth beast, the one seen, is the kingdom of Ishmael; it is the one likened in Nebuchadnezzar's dream to iron, and in the prophecy it is written: 'and it had iron teeth.' He did not mention this fourth beast in the second prophecy or in the fourth, but only in this prophecy did he explain its matters until the coming of the redeemer. And in the second prophecy he explained the matter of the third beast and completed all its matters until the coming of the redeemer, for in the days of these two kingdoms [the redeemer] will come, as he mentioned in the dream: 'and in the days of those kings.'" "<b>And the meaning of 'ten horns'</b> — that the kingdom of Ishmael spread throughout most of the inhabited world, and these are the horns: the kingdom of Baghdad, and the kingdom of Isfahan, and the kingdom of the Yemenites, that is, Saba, and the kingdom of Mecca, that is, Mišaʿ according to the Gaon [Saadia]. And the kingdom of Egypt, and the kingdom of Africa, and the kingdom of the Ishmaelites who dwell in tents in the east and in the west, and the kingdom of the Philistines, who are the Almoravids, and the kingdom of the Berbers, who are sons of Ham and they are white, and the kingdom of the Cushites, and they are many kings. And all of these have one Torah, and the matter of the little horn is still future, for this will be close to the coming of the redeemer, as I shall explain. And this horn is a nation that shall come forth from the east that will return to the Torah of these horns and will destroy three kingdoms. And this king will be wise and speak great things. Then shall be cast down the thrones of all the kings of the nations. And this shall be at the standing of Michael, the great prince, as shall be explained, and He is the Ancient of Days; he saw him in the visions of prophecy as though he were old." "<b>Thrones</b> — it is His throne." "<b>And His wheels</b> — they are the spheres, and from the abundance of their course sparks of fire go out, for the sphere of fire is beneath the sphere of the moon, by clear proofs. Do not wonder at 'a thousand thousands minister unto Him,' for all is by the command of HaShem, the honored and supreme One. Do you not see that Michael is called the great prince, and under him are ministers, and they are the host of heaven, which are the host of HaShem? And thus it is written: 'I am the prince of the host of YHWH,' that the awesome Name is attached to 'hosts,' which stand always and do not cease, as I explained in the Book of the Honored Name. And further I shall reveal a little of the secret of the holy angels to those who understand. Now he saw that HaShem executes judgment and judges all the earth, and the books were open before Him — after the manner of one who counts what one has written — and it is written in a book of remembrance before Him. And regarding the matter of the angels, I shall speak of this. And indeed he explained that he saw, in that 'the beast was slain,' that the entire kingdom of Ishmael shall perish in a brief moment, in a few days." "<b>And the rest of the beasts</b> — their dominion was taken away — for the first beasts, the kingship of each was removed and their bodies remained. But this fourth beast, its body shall be destroyed entirely, and no survivor or fugitive of Ishmael shall remain. And Rabbi Yeshua said: this 'one like a son of man' is the Messiah. And the matter is correct, but it is the holy people, who are Israel." "<b>And to him was given</b> — from this verse you can learn that everything done on earth is decrees of heaven. And I said that this 'one like a son of man' is Israel, which is the name of the species, because Daniel said concerning the Ancient of Days: 'and judgment was given to the holy ones of the Most High.' And the meaning is to take vengeance on the fourth beast." "<b>And the word 'it was destroyed'</b> — it has no parallel except for 'in a scabbard' (בגו נדנה), for the body is to the spirit like a scabbard to a sword, as: 'and he returned his sword to its scabbard.' And the meaning is as though it departed from sheer terror."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The quotation from Saadia is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The phrase 'ומנדעי יתוב עלי' is obscure and possibly corrupt.", 3 "The place name אצפהן is resolved as Isfahan; אלימן as Yemenites; מיכא/מישא left in transliteration per Ibn Ezra's argument referencing Saadia."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], 